{"kind":"propose","text":"REVISED DECISION PROPOSAL — MAX-FAN-OUT IS RELATIVE INCREMENTAL APPEND COST.\n\nThis replaces retired proposal 3db9488e and accepts every correction in ratified changes-requested report 30c47f5b.\n\nDecision. The max-fan-out target measures how much causal bases add to an otherwise identical append. It does not measure total append latency. Signing, Git publication, sequencer admission, verification and folding are paid at one base and belong to the separate fixed-append target.\n\nContract-native measurement. Use performance/contract-v1.json unchanged and the full tier: generator version and seed from the contract, linear one-actor fixture, submit_ack fan-out cases at the fan-out axis depth selected by perflane.BenchmarkCases, currently depth 1,000, fan-outs 1, 8, 16, 64 and 256, five warmups and 100 recorded repetitions per case. The cases are separate distributions; do not invent cross-case round pairing. For each width f, report the signed relative increment median(T_f)/median(T_1)-1 from the same retained run, together with each distribution, raw samples, exact head, contract and fixture digests, case order and environment. Do not clamp negative estimates. A sample that fails the harness trusted-versus-projected digest check is an error and invalidates the run; equality in a completed sample is a validity precondition, not evidence that the performance change preserves correctness.\n\nBound. PREVIEW passes its fan-out dimension only when the signed median ratio at 64 bases is at most 1.10 and every measured width through 64 is at most 1.10. FIRST-PRODUCTION passes its fan-out dimension only when the ratio at 256 bases is at most 1.10 and every measured width through 256 is at most 1.10. In plain English, causal fan-out may add no more than ten percent to the median cost already paid by a one-base append, and an intermediate nonlinear jump also fails. The ten-percent allowance is a product budget, parallel to the envelope table actor-count allowance; it is not fitted to the observed slope or the instrument noise. As fixed append cost falls, the allowed fan-out milliseconds fall with it.\n\nLoad and uncertainty. The decision makes no claim that an absolute latency difference cancels load. A ratio is invariant only to a common multiplicative factor; changing load between case blocks can still bias it and must be disclosed rather than called cancellation. The contract count replaces the rejected seven-sample bespoke protocol. If a retained run is visibly split across different load regimes or another full run changes the pass/fail classification, the result is inconclusive and must be rerun; the raw distributions remain the evidence.\n\nAxis meaning. The committed contract intentionally measures scale dimensions independently and pins fan-out to depth 1,000 rather than multiplying every width by every sequence depth. A passing ratio therefore establishes the PREVIEW and FIRST-PRODUCTION fan-out dimensions at their exact maximum widths, not an end-to-end append guarantee at depth 50,000 or 500,000. The existing depth-1,000 and depth-10,000 reproductions support, but do not prove across the whole envelope, the claim that incremental fan-out cost is independent of fixed fold depth. Documentation must say this plainly. A cross-product claim would require a separately reviewed versioned-contract change and evidence at the envelope depth.\n\nCurrent evidence. The workroom medians give 773.7/764.0 = 1.0127 at 256 bases. Codex depth-1,000 medians give 519.902/527.782 = 0.9851. Claude depth-1,000 medians give 999.3/994.3 = 1.0050, and depth-10,000 gives 2527.3/2627.3 = 0.9619. These signed central estimates all sit inside 1.10 and agree that fixed cost dominates, but their six- or seven-round custom runs are corroboration, not the formal 100-sample contract verdict. The assigned evidence-and-documentation loop must produce the retained contract-full classification before the page labels the target pass.\n\nSeparate absolute goal. The 50 ms absolute append goal remains a fixed one-base submit_ack product target. Existing request 8add6909 remains parked: nobody is authorized by this proposal to claim or implement it before this decision is adopted and its basis is repaired. It is not a substitute for the fan-out ratio and the ratio is not a substitute for it.\n\nContracts and simplification. This decision changes measurement attribution only. It cannot be met by deferring or removing actor signing, sequencer admission, verified-ref compare-and-swap, signature or bound verification, complete fold semantics, idempotency, trusted-versus-projected equality, error behavior or atomic publication. It uses the committed lane instead of a parallel hand-built protocol. No architecture contract changes. This proposal governs only after authorized ratifier adoption and successful independent review."}